# Scratch screenshots land at the repo ROOT (design mockups, review captures).
# Leading slash on purpose: PNGs that are real assets live inside packages
# (web/public, docs/) and must stay tracked.
/*.png

# Written when MUXPAD_DATA_DIR is the literal string "undefined" (a harness
# env leak, not a real data dir). Never an artifact worth tracking.
server/undefined/

# Standalone credential broker dependencies
broker/node_modules/

# THIS MACHINE'S BROKER RELEASES, not source. It pins the release hashes and
# the tailnet `origin` of the host they were built for — a real machine name
# in a PUBLIC repo, and meaningless to anyone else's install. `setupReleases`
# already returns [] when the file is absent, so a fresh checkout simply
# offers no setup commands until it has its own.
server/assets/slack-setup-releases.json
